      "summaries": {
        "en": "MediaCrawler is a Python-based web scraping tool that simplifies data collection from major Chinese social media platforms like Xiaohongshu, Douyin, and Bilibili, addressing the challenge of accessing structured content for analysis. Its technical strength lies in handling platform-specific anti-scraping measures through modular design, allowing targeted adaptation. Users can deploy it via command-line interfaces or integrate its APIs into custom pipelines for tasks like sentiment analysis, trend monitoring, or academic research on digital behavior.",
        "zh": "MediaCrawler 是一个专注于中文社交媒体平台的 Python 爬虫工具，它能高效地从小红书、抖音、B站等网站抓取笔记、视频和评论数据，解决了手动收集网络内容费时费力的问题。其技术亮点在于采用模块化设计来应对不同平台的反爬机制，开发者可以灵活调整策略以稳定获取数据。实践上，用户可通过命令行快速启动数据采集，或将其 API 集成到自己的分析流程中，用于市场调研、舆情分析或学术研究，为理解在线社区动态提供可靠的数据基础。",
        "es": "MediaCrawler is a Python-based web scraping tool that simplifies data collection from major Chinese social media platforms like Xiaohongshu, Douyin, and Bilibili, addressing the challenge of accessing structured content for analysis. Its technical strength lies in handling platform-specific anti-scraping measures through modular design, allowing targeted adaptation. Users can deploy it via command-line interfaces or integrate its APIs into custom pipelines for tasks like sentiment analysis, trend monitoring, or academic research on digital behavior.",
        "sections": {
          "why": "MediaCrawler gives teams a dependable path to production-ready AI tooling.",
          "what": "MediaCrawler is a Python-based web scraping tool that simplifies data collection from major Chinese social media platforms like Xiaohongshu, Douyin, and Bilibili, addressing the challenge of accessing structured content for analysis. Its technical strength lies in handling platform-specific anti-scraping measures through modular design, allowing targeted adaptation. Users can deploy it via command-line interfaces or integrate its APIs into custom pipelines for tasks like sentiment analysis, trend monitoring, or academic research on digital behavior.",
          "how": "Review https://github.com/NanmiCoder/MediaCrawler for docs, run starter examples, and integrate with your pipeline or evaluation stack."
        }
      },
